<Programs>
<Program Name="MainProgram" TestEdits="false" Disabled="false">
<Tags/>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="InView" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[All information provided  - No Warranty or implied merchantability. 
Refer to the RSLogix 5000 End User License Agreement (EULA) in the Release Notes.

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Message Number Enter from the PV+ is intended to toggle the next message number.
The Message Number From PV is the message number that will be . 
Remember, the Controller does not  the message, it is the InView Message display that polls for a 0 to 1 transition. ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Message_No_Enter)[MOV(Message_No_From_PV,Message_Number) ,OTE(Message_No_Enter_HS) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Variable 1,2 and 3 are grouped together to display one  value with a fixed decimal at two places.  The decimal is part of the message text.
To display 89.45:
Variable 1 is the whole part of the number (89)
Variable 2 is the 10ths place (4)
Variable 3 is the 100ths place (5).
It takes all three Variables and three triggers to display the number 89.45.
Keep in mind that the variables in the message are configured not to display zeros in front of the number (i.e. None:1). ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Variable_0_Enter)[MOV(Variable_0_From_PV,Variable_Data_0) ,OTE(Variable_0_Enter_HS) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Variable_1_Enter)[MOV(Variable_1_From_PV,Variable_Data_1) ,OTE(Variable_1_Enter_HS) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Message Enter Pushbutton is toggled to  the message.
The transition from 0 to 1 of Message_SINT[0].0  the message.
The InView Display polls for this transition at the value in the InterScan Delay.
The on to off time must be greater thant the InterScan Delay.  The InterScan Delay is set in \the Communications Setup and is downloaded to the InView communications module.  This file is a *ivc file.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Message_No_Enter) ONS(OneShots[0]) ,XIC(Messsage_Trigger.EN) ]XIO(Message_Trigger_Off_Time.DN)[TON(Messsage_Trigger,?,?) ,XIC(Messsage_Trigger.DN) OTE(Message_SINT[0].0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Messsage_Trigger.DN)TON(Message_Trigger_Off_Time,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Variable_Trigger_Off_Time.DN)[TON(Variable_Trigger_On_Time,?,?) ,XIC(Variable_Trigger_On_Time.DN) OTE(Variable_SINT[0].0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Variable_Trigger_On_Time.DN)TON(Variable_Trigger_Off_Time,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung is used to convert the Message_Number, Function and Display Address to a String.  This is done because it is easier to manipulate string data than integer data.
Message_Number=DINT
Message Function=DINT
Display Address=DINT (Power up the Inview and determine the Display Address, the default is 248)
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[DTOS(Message_Number,InView_Message_String[1])DTOS(Function,InView_Message_String[5])DTOS(Display_Address,InView_Message_String[9]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
</Programs>
